<!-- One entry per route in js/routes.js. Keep the two in step: a URL listed
     here that the deploy does not answer is a soft 404, and a route missing
     from here is one Google has to find on its own.

     Each of these is now a real file (projects.html, certs.html, about.html,
     contact.html, generated by tools/build-routes.mjs) with its own title,
     description and self-referencing canonical. Before that they all served
     index.html and all claimed to be "/", so this file was listing five URLs
     that the HTML itself insisted were one page. Sitelinks are drawn from a
     site's other INDEXED pages, so that had to stop being true first.

     priority is a hint about relative importance WITHIN this site; it has no
     bearing on ranking against anyone else. The order matches the nav. -->
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
